WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.502
This slide brings Module 2 together.

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:06.257
Review the patterns you can now recognize and reuse.

00:00:06.257 --> 00:00:12.122
Focus on the decisions behind the syntax: what structure or method fits the problem,

00:00:12.122 --> 00:00:18.377
what assumptions are being made, and what you should check before trusting the result.

00:00:18.377 --> 00:00:23.812
In real analytics, this pattern can support thresholds, validation rules, category assignment, alerts,

00:00:23.812 --> 00:00:24.802
and repeated processing.

00:00:24.802 --> 00:00:32.792
The examples are intentionally small so you can trace the logic from the condition to the result.

00:00:32.792 --> 00:00:38.552
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:38.552 --> 00:00:43.973
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
